			"Message": "fix(Output): Refactor drag and maximize commands to use typed window API\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "50f88d74a0a3bd374dfee91b10cc5532c1e276a9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T18:18:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Use typed window API for drag/maximize with explicit label\n\nThe generic `InvokeWindowCommand(command:string)` dispatched bare `core.invoke` calls without the window `label` payload. Tauri 2.x's IPC dispatcher silently drops `plugin:window|start_dragging` invocations when no window label is provided and no window matches the implicit context — the overlay-titlebar window never moved. The typed JS API (`Window.startDragging()`, `Window.toggleMaximize()`) transparently injects the correct label from the caller's window handle.\n\nSplit `InvokeWindowCommand` into `StartDragging` and `ToggleMaximize`, each preferring the typed window API first, then falling back to raw `invoke` with an explicit `{ label }` payload. The label is resolved from `getCurrentWindow().label`, `getCurrentWebviewWindow().label`, or the literal `\"main\"` as last resort.\n\nBoth drag-initiation and titlebar double-click maximize now work reliably under Tauri 2.",
			"SHA": "79a2a5f8b62f91f4c725b13521911fa62e697e61"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T17:56:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Activate drag via mousedown capture when Tauri fails to intercept\n\nTauri 2's own drag listener only activates under the `tauri://` protocol; Land's webview loads from `http://localhost:21100`, so the `data-tauri-drag-region` attribute alone is insufficient to initiate window movement. Add a capture-phase `mousedown` handler that walks the ancestor chain for the drag attribute and dispatches `plugin:window|start_dragging` (single click) or `internal_toggle_maximize` (double click) via the Tauri invoke API with multiple fallback paths (core.invoke, __TAURI_INTERNALS__, window API).\n\nIncludes `IsDragTarget()` for ancestor-chain attribute detection and `InvokeWindowCommand()` with graceful fallbacks for both modern and legacy Tauri 2 surfaces.",
			"SHA": "6b6dbbde3b73cef39eb647182977425ba6fef3ed"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T17:21:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				15
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Align Tauri commands and expose IOutputService for panel\n\nOverhaul the Output element's Tauri command routing and drag-region polyfill to match Tauri 2's actual command surface and WKWebView behaviour:\n\n- **Process commands to snake_case:** Rename all ProcessTauri invocations (`ProcessGetExecPath` -> `process_get_exec_path`, etc.) because Tauri 2 passes the literal Rust function name without auto-camel conversion. The PascalCase names produced `Command not found` errors.\n\n- **Update service to Mountain dispatch names:** Rename `update:check` -> `update:checkForUpdates`, `update:download` -> `update:downloadUpdate`, `update:install` -> `update:applyUpdate`, `update:get_status` -> `update:_getInitialState` so they match Mountain's `IPC/WindServiceHandlers` dispatcher arms. The previous short names silently failed with no matching handler.\n\n- **Expose IOutputService in CEL accessor:** Resolve `IOutputService` alongside existing services so Sky's `sky://output/append` bridge can call `Output?.getChannel(id)?.append(text)` to write into the actual Output panel instead of the diagnostic console sink.\n\n- **Refactor drag-region polyfill to build-time extraction:** Replace runtime stylesheet-walking (which fails under WKWebView because `CSSStyleRule.style.getPropertyValue` returns empty for `-webkit-app-region`) with a build-time transform that scans VS Code CSS files via regex and bakes selector arrays into the bundle as `globalThis.__LAND_DRAG_SELECTORS__` / `__LAND_NO_DRAG_SELECTORS__`. Strip CSS comments from extracted selectors before splitting on commas to handle upstream banner comments in selector lists.\n\n- **Add mousedown drag listener:** Install a capture-phase `mousedown` on `document` that walks the ancestor chain for the `data-tauri-drag-region` attribute and dispatches `start_dragging` (single click) or `internal_toggle_maximize` (double click). Tauri's own drag listener is only injected under the `tauri://` protocol; Land's webview loads from `http://localhost:21100`, so the attribute alone was insufficient.\n\nAll four subsystems (drag polyfill, process info, update flow, output service) now correctly interoperate with Tauri 2's runtime and Mountain's handler surface.",
			"SHA": "6a999f8691463cb9d9aee5b866b83a5f626052e7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T15:16:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				765,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Rename Tauri health commands to snake_case for Tauri 2\n\nTauri 2 passes the command name as the literal Rust function name without auto-camel conversion. The PascalCase names (`CocoonExtensionHostHealth`, `CocoonSearchServiceHealth`, `CocoonDebugServiceHealth`, `SharedProcessServiceHealth`) produced `Command not found` errors at runtime.\n\nRename to snake_case in the Shared Process proxy's `healthCheck()` to match the actual handler function names registered in Mountain's health command modules.\n\nAll four per-service health checks now resolve correctly under Tauri 2's strict command-name matching.",
			"SHA": "c30a934e5ba5ac7fae7a30efecf0924e1ce67385"
		}
	],
